B.anM=new A.rl("Longitudinal Sweep","Place the probe vertically on the midline of the abdomen just above the pubic bone. Slide slowly upward toward the fundus in a straight line. Keep the probe flat and maintain gentle, consistent pressure.","Midline \u2014 Pubic bone to Fundus","Parallel to spine (0\xb0)","Uterine outline, fetal spine, placenta position","Placenta previa (placenta covering cervix)",B.a_N)
B.a07=new A.at(58917,"MaterialIcons",null,!1)
B.anL=new A.rl("Transverse Upper Sweep","Rotate probe 90\xb0 to lie horizontally. Position at the fundus (top of the uterus). Slide slowly downward across the upper half of the abdomen.","Transverse \u2014 Fundus","Perpendicular to spine (90\xb0)","Fetal head or breech, amniotic fluid pockets","Transverse lie, oligohydramnios",B.a07)
B.a_T=new A.at(57938,"MaterialIcons",null,!1)
B.anN=new A.rl("Fetal Head View","Locate the fetal head. Tilt and rock the probe gently to get the head in cross-section. Look for the oval shape with the midline echo and thalami. Freeze the image when the standard plane is achieved.","Over fetal head \u2014 variable","Angled to head plane","Biparietal diameter (BPD), cavum septum pellucidum, thalami","Hydrocephalus (enlarged ventricles), abnormal head shape",B.a_T)
B.a0h=new A.at(61267,"MaterialIcons",null,!1)
B.anK=new A.rl("Abdominal Circumference View","Move probe to mid-abdomen. Tilt to find the transverse section of the fetal abdomen. Look for the stomach bubble on the left and the umbilical vein. This is a round cross-section \u2014 freeze when stomach + UV are both visible.","Mid-abdomen transverse","Perpendicular to fetal spine","Stomach bubble, umbilical vein, circular abdomen outline","Absent stomach bubble (possible esophageal atresia), ascites",B.a0h)
B.a06=new A.at(58894,"MaterialIcons",null,!1)
B.anJ=new A.rl("Femur Length","Locate a fetal thigh. Align the probe along the long axis of the femur. The femur should appear as a bright horizontal line with acoustic shadow below. Measure from greater trochanter to lateral condyle.","Over fetal thigh \u2014 variable","Along femur long axis","Linear bright femur shaft, both ends visible","Short femur for gestational age, fracture, bowing",B.a06)
B.a0X=new A.at(984482,"MaterialIcons",null,!1)
B.anI=new A.rl("Placenta & Fluid Check","Do a final sweep along the uterine wall to locate the full placenta. Note its position (anterior, posterior, fundal). Then identify the largest vertical pocket of amniotic fluid for AFI.","Follow placenta location","Parallel to uterine wall","Placental tissue (grainy texture), largest fluid pocket","Placenta previa, retroplacental clot, AFI < 2cm or > 8cm",B.a0X)
